From 27be24c9dc3b033dca8681315691a056adec2ba6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fieldmar <974888+fieldmar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:43:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] camellia: patch the MTK Codec2 HAL's dequeueBuffer fence leak

android.hardware.media.c2@1.2-mediatek leaks the release fence that
dequeueBuffer hands it: one sync_file per displayed frame, never
closed. At 30 fps it hits the 32768-fd limit after about 18 minutes of
video, aborts ("Failed to clone native_handle in hidl_handle: Too many
open files") and restarts, so the app's decoder dies with DEAD_OBJECT.
In YouTube Shorts the picture jumps to the next clip while the captions
stay.

Add a frameworks/av patch that wraps the producer handed to the HAL in
client.cpp so dequeueBuffer waits on the fence on the framework side
and passes no fence to the HAL. Document it in patches/README.md.

Verified 2026-11-22: HAL fd count stays flat at about 160 with no
sync_file entries while Shorts play, and 20+ minutes of Shorts with no
skip.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Ibd24b3cffc4ddb6b98d0231ab9e963d73d618cd1
